  "observations": [
    "Clamped sources through degree16 can use the shared initial endpoint-tangent cubic across multiple spans when there are no resolved G1 tangent breaks. The shared classifier removes offsets and uses binary scaling, as in region matching; existing G2 chart matching is retained.",
    "Curvature changes alone do not require separate fits. Positional jumps and resolved tangent corners retain their existing policies. An independent complete positional bound cannot erase those policies.",
    "Every admitted profile still requires a complete exact certificate within half the requested tolerance. Mapped correspondence covers all source and candidate intervals, not just sampled points. Endpoint chords must exceed the tolerance.",
    "A common-handle correction can make the quarter-degree polyline satisfy the positional bound while Rhino still subdivides it. That experiment was rejected; correction remains qualified only for single-Bezier sources. Multispan initial failures retain explicit errors.",
    "The new API corpus admits30 records and retains36 native subdivision cases. Six command records also match. Existing corpora gain22 angle-overload matches and6 polygon matches; earlier matching, single-span correction and subdivision limits remain unchanged.",
    "Three analytical checks exercise complete multispan bounds, preservation of resolved corners and positional jumps, and an interior bump invisible at endpoints and midpoint. A command regression preserves selection, sources and redo history after a tighter fit fails."
  ],
